  "representational_boundaries": {
    "canonical_path_count": 5,
    "no_sixth_path": "The frozen sources support no no-rehearing counterfactual mandate and no stay-grant/dissolution branch; the corpus therefore contains exactly five executions rather than a standard six-path shape.",
    "sealed_session_separation": "The workflow and canonical traces bind only public record entries. Sealed twins remain available solely through the record disclosure-session boundary and never enter a workflow command or event provenance selector.",
    "b14_response_request": "The Rule 40(d)(4) request for a response is an unbound court-authorized stage advance because the frozen record contains no separate docketed request order; B14 remains the generic motion filing bound to the response route.",
    "b12_b27_engine_boundary": "B12 is the sole counterfactual issue_judgment operation. B21 vacates its opinion and judgment as a source event, but the engine has no judgment-reset opcode; B27 is therefore an exact enter_order revised-judgment binding and the stored engine judgment SHA intentionally remains B12 through B28."
  },
